This looks like leftovers: a plate with some remaining lasagna (about 100 g) and a second plate with a small piece of meat (about 15 g). The glass holds water, which adds no calories.

Lasagna runs about 150 kcal per 100 g, so 100 g is roughly 150 kcal. The meat is about 20 g of roast or braised meat at roughly 2 kcal/g, so about 40 kcal. That brings the total to roughly 190 kcal. Combined mass is about 120 g.

